      "text": "### Book Information\n**Title:** Stochastic Governance: Probabilistic Approaches to Policy Design Under Uncertainty  \n**Authors:** Vasilis Papadimitriou and Sakura Nishihara  \n**Year:** 2021  \n**Publisher:** MIT Policy Press  \n**ISBN:** 978-0-26203-847-1  \n**Summary:** This 312-page technical monograph applies Bayesian inference and stochastic optimization to the design of public policies in the face of deep uncertainty. The authors argue that traditional policy analysis frameworks, which rely on deterministic projections and point estimates, tend to underperform in scenarios marked by non-stationary risks and contested model assumptions. They propose an 'adaptive policy envelope' framework, where policy commitments are treated as probability distributions over possible outcomes instead of fixed prescriptions. This approach allows for policies to be updated based on new evidence without compromising credibility. The book includes detailed case studies on climate adaptation policy in the Netherlands, design of pandemic response protocols, and infrastructure investment under seismic risk.  \n**Key Themes:** Bayesian policy analysis, deep uncertainty, adaptive governance, stochastic optimization, policy design, decision theory, uncertainty quantification.\n\n### Author Profiles\n\n#### Vasilis Papadimitriou\n- **Position:** Professor of Public Policy at Harvard Kennedy School\n- **Research Focus:** Bayesian policy analysis, adaptive governance, and deep uncertainty.\n- **Education:** PhD in Operations Research from MIT, 2003.\n- **Notable Publications:**\n  - \"Stochastic Governance\" (MIT Policy Press, 2021)\n  - \"Adaptive Policy Envelopes under Deep Uncertainty\" (Policy Sciences, 2018)\n  - \"Bayesian Updating in Multi-Stakeholder Policy Contexts\" (Journal of Policy Analysis and Management, 2015)\n  - Co-editor of \"Uncertainty and Governance: A Reader\" (MIT Press, 2019)\n- **More Information:** [Vasilis Papadimitriou - Harvard Kennedy School 